WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.635
[music playing]

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:08.174
This is, like, pretty legit.

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.442
That's, like, a long ways.

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:11.378
I'm pretty pleased
you're saying that.

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:13.046
I'm definitely feeling it.

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:16.049
I mean, this is
300 feet at least.

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:19.486
Ultimately we want to
get down into the gorge.

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:21.187
Let's rappel off the bridge?

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:24.858
Yeah that's a great idea.

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:35.235
[music playing]

00:00:39.406 --> 00:00:42.175
This is, like, pretty legit.

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:47.347
Ultimately we want to
get down into the gorge.

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:50.083
Free solo climber
Alex Honnold and I

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.318
are high up in the Swiss
Alps, trying to get

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:53.953
to the bottom of this ravine.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.789
Let's rappel off the bridge.

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:02.262
That's a great idea.

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:05.565
All right, can we
try and do from here?

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:06.433
Are you sure?

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:07.600
Do we have this much rope?

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:08.435
Yeah.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:10.236
We're going to need this.

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:12.505
We're going to need the
extra length and also

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:14.674
the emergency length as well.

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:16.643
[music playing]

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:24.984
So what we're going to
do, counterbalanced repel.

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:27.220
You go one side, I go the other.

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:29.823
As long as we go at the same
time it's going to work.

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:31.991
Right and as long as we
have twice as much rope.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:35.395
This is a technique that
the special forces use a lot

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:37.230
because it's fast and
it doesn't actually

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:38.998
require anything to anchor to.

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:43.002
But we're going to need all
of our rope and the spare rope

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:44.771
to reach the bottom of this one.

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:48.541
This will be about a 300
foot counterbalanced repel.

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:51.911
And by using the same rope,
Alex and I will attempt

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:54.214
to descend simultaneously.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.182
But if one of us puts
weight on the rope

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:58.351
without the counterweight
of the other person,

00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:01.287
Alex or I could plummet to
the bottom of this ravine.

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:03.723
So we've got to make sure
we go at the same time

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:08.161
and maintain the same
speed during our descent.

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:10.597
The thing is, what
I do know is there's

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:13.633
going to be a lot of
friction still on these bits.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.802
And that is the sort of
stuff that can cut rope.

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:19.005
So I do want to do
something that protects us.

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:21.207
Any spare socks?

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:23.977
I mean, I guess you
could use my socks.

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:25.211
Grab them, there's
some of in the bag.

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:26.079
You got any spare ones?

00:02:26.145 --> 00:02:27.580
Yeah, for tonight.

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:29.916
There's a lot of abrasion
on these wires, little bits

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:31.484
of metal sticking up.

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:33.686
They're just the sort of thing
that would cut through rope

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:36.956
really easily, especially if
we start bouncing on this thing

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:38.291
as we're descending.

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:42.161
So I reckon if we put
over the top of that.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:45.064
That is a very
improvised rope protector.

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:46.266
I think it's good.

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:48.868
It's going to run through that.

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:52.939
OK, this is the most bomb
repel of my entire life.

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:54.774
This is totally amazing.

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:55.675
OK, here we go.

00:02:58.044 --> 00:03:00.346
This feels suspiciously
like jumping out of the plane.

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:04.217
Like, here we go.

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:06.686
OK, so we've got to
go at the same time.

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:08.288
Yep.

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:11.391
All right so,
maybe not too much

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:13.593
at the same time so don't
wreck each other's [bleep]..

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:14.227
You ready?

00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:17.630
3, 2, 1, see you.

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:20.133
[music playing]

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:24.170
Should we stay a
little bit apart?

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:26.472
Yeah, like this is good.

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:28.308
[music playing]

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:31.811
So bouncy.

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:35.949
Yeah, that's why I put
the rope protection in here.

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:37.817
[music playing]

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:41.988
OK, we'll get a bit
middle speed now.

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:43.990
OK.

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:49.028
Whoo, see, most
of the time I have

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:51.130
to go super slow with guests.

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:52.265
This is great.

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:54.400
[music playing]

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:01.841
That was a fricking
amazing repel.

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:02.675
Yeah.

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:04.077
That's awesome.

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:05.912
It's a long ways.

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:07.113
That's a pleasure.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:10.083
That's a lovely
repel, it's super fun.

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:12.719
I think the socks add
some nice padding.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:13.786
That's how you do it.

